Start the guest with the signal state of a fresh login

An Android app starts PRoot with SIGHUP ignored and SIGQUIT, SIGUSR1,
SIGPIPE and glibc's internal signal blocked (the app's own
/proc/self/status: SigIgn 0x1, SigBlk 0x80001204). Ignored dispositions
and the blocked mask both survive fork(2) and execve(2), so every guest
process inherited them: `kill -HUP` could not end a job, a closing
terminal could not hang one up, and a blocked SIGPIPE stayed pending
instead of ending the writer. Upstream already resets SIGPIPE's
disposition at this point; this resets every ignored disposition and
the mask as well.

Upstream: termux/proot v5.1.107.92, after 0002. Applied by
app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.

--- a/src/tracee/event.c
+++ b/src/tracee/event.c
@@ -81,6 +81,28 @@
  * Start @tracee->exe with the given @argv[].  This function
  * returns -errno if an error occurred, otherwise 0.
  */
+/**
+ * Give the calling process the signal state of a fresh login: nothing
+ * ignored, nothing blocked.
+ */
+static void reset_signal_state()
+{
+	sigset_t nothing;
+	int signum;
+
+	for (signum = 1; signum < NSIG; signum++) {
+		struct sigaction current;
+
+		if (signum == SIGKILL || signum == SIGSTOP)
+			continue;
+		if (sigaction(signum, NULL, &current) == 0 && current.sa_handler == SIG_IGN)
+			signal(signum, SIG_DFL);
+	}
+
+	sigemptyset(&nothing);
+	sigprocmask(SIG_SETMASK, &nothing, NULL);
+}
+
 int launch_process(Tracee *tracee, char *const argv[])
 {
 	char *const default_argv[] = { "-sh", NULL };
@@ -114,6 +136,17 @@
 		 * system, like container runtimes do.  */
 		signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL);
 
+		/* The same goes for everything else an Android app
+		 * hands down: its runtime ignores SIGHUP and blocks
+		 * SIGQUIT, SIGUSR1, SIGPIPE and the signal glibc uses
+		 * for thread cancellation (measured in the app's
+		 * /proc/self/status: SigIgn 0x1, SigBlk 0x80001204).
+		 * Inherited, a hangup could not end a job and a blocked
+		 * SIGPIPE stayed pending instead of ending the writer.
+		 * No handler is installed yet at this point, so every
+		 * disposition is either the default or ignored.  */
+		reset_signal_state();
+
 		/* Declare myself as ptraceable before executing the
 		 * requested program. */
 		status = ptrace(PTRACE_TRACEME, 0, NULL, NULL);
